#. type: Title =
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/game-values.adoc:2
#, no-wrap
msgid "Game Values"
msgstr "Termes de Jeu"

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/game-values.adoc:8
msgid ""
"Before progressing to the rules of the game, we will categorise the "
"different kinds of troops, and assign suitable game values to each."
msgstr ""
"Avant de poursuivre les règles du jeu, nous allons catégoriser les "
"différents types de troupes et définir en terme de jeu chacune d'elles."

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/game-values.adoc:20
msgid ""
"A game of Warmaster is played between two opposing model armies. Each side "
"is controlled by a single player who plans and executes his army’s moves and "
"rolls dice as required to determine the results of movement and fighting."
msgstr ""
"Une partie de Warmaster se joue entre deux armées de figurines adverses. "
"Chaque camp est contrôlé par un seul joueur qui planifie et exécute les "
"mouvements de son armée et lance les dés nécessaires pour déterminer les "
"résultats des mouvements et des combats."

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/game-values.adoc:35
msgid ""
"The playing pieces of the game are called *stands*.  There are two kinds of "
"stands: 40mm × 20mm unit stands and [.edit]#character stands, often round "
"and 25mm in diameter# [.ancients]#in order to readily distinguish them from "
"troop stands.# [.edit]#(See xref:characters.adoc#odd-size-character-"
"bases[Odd size character bases] if you have characters mounted on larger "
"bases.)#"
msgstr ""
"Les pièces du jeu sont appelées *socles*. Il existe deux types de socles : "
"les socles d'unité de 40 mm × 20 mm et les [.edit]#socles de personnage, "
"souvent ronds et de 25 mm de diamètre# [.ancients]#afin de les distinguer "
"facilement des socles de troupe.# [.edit]#(Voir xref:characters.adoc#odd-"
"size-character-bases[Socles de personnage de taille inhabituelle] si vous "
"avez des personnages sur des socles plus grands.)#"

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/game-values.adoc:41
msgid ""
"Models are mounted onto the stands so that they form representative bodies "
"of troops or characters. The actual number of models and their positioning "
"is a matter of aesthetic choice and is left up to players."
msgstr ""
"Les figurines sont montées sur les socles afin de former des groupes "
"représentatifs de troupes ou de personnages. Le nombre exact de figurines et "
"leur positionnement relèvent du choix esthétique des joueurs."

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/game-values.adoc:47
msgid ""
"All unit stands have front, side and rear edges as indicated by the "
"direction faced by the models. It is important that the direction faced by "
"the stand is obvious as in the examples below."
msgstr ""
"Tous les socles d'unités ont des bords avant, latéraux et arrière, indiqués "
"par l'orientation des figurines. Il est important que l'orientation du socle "
"soit clairement visible, comme dans les exemples ci-dessous."

#. type: Title ==
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/game-values.adoc:50
#, no-wrap
msgid "Units"
msgstr "Unités"

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/game-values.adoc:60
msgid ""
"Infantry, cavalry and most other types of troops fight in formations of "
"several stands [.ancients]#called *units*#.  A number of stands form a "
"regiment of infantry, a squadron of cavalry, a battery of artillery, and so "
"on.  All the stands in the same formation are always arranged so they are "
"touching, either side-by-side, one behind the other, or contacting at a "
"point. [.ancients]#This is referred to as a *formation*.#"
msgstr ""
"L'infanterie, la cavalerie et la plupart des autres types de troupes "
"combattent en formations de plusieurs socles [.ancients]#appelées *unités*#. "
"Plusieurs socles forment un régiment d'infanterie, un escadron de cavalerie, "
"une batterie d'artillerie, etc. Tous les socles d'une même formation sont "
"toujours disposés de manière à se toucher, soit côte à côte, soit l'un "
"derrière l'autre, soit en se touchant en un seul point. [.ancients]#On parle "
"alors de *formation*.#"

#. //Removed WMR:
#. For convenience, we shall refer to all of these formations as *units*.
#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/game-values.adoc:69
msgid ""
"Units usually consist of three stands of the same type but this can vary and "
"sometimes a unit can be just a single stand, as we shall see later."
msgstr ""
"Les unités se composent généralement de trois socles du même type, mais cela "
"peut varier et parfois une unité peut ne comporter qu'un seul socle, comme "
"nous le verrons plus tard."

#. // Removed WMR (from box)
#. Troops are arranged into units consisting of a number of
#. ‘stands’ – usually three but sometimes two or even just
#. one. This page shows typical infantry and cavalry units.
#.  TODO Remove/move later (WMR)
#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/game-values.adoc:81
msgid ""
"Up to four units can be temporarily placed together to form a *brigade*. "
"We’ll be covering brigades in much more detail in the rules that follow."
msgstr ""
"Jusqu'à quatre unités peuvent être temporairement regroupées pour former une "
"brigade. Nous aborderons les brigades plus en détail dans les règles "
"suivantes."

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/game-values.adoc:91
msgid ""
"In addition to the troops described, armies always include a General and can "
"include other Heroes and Wizards as well. These consist of a single stand "
"which includes the mighty individual as well as assorted helpmates and "
"hangers on. These stands are referred to as characters."
msgstr ""
"Outre les troupes décrites, les armées comprennent toujours un Général et "
"peuvent également inclure d'autres Héros et Sorciers. Elles sont constituées "
"d'un seul socle comprenant le puissant personnage ainsi que divers "
"compagnons et serviteurs. Ces socles sont appelés personnages."

#. type: Title ==
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/game-values.adoc:95
#, no-wrap
msgid "Infantry, cavalry, chariots, monsters, artillery & machines"
msgstr "Infanterie, cavalerie, chars, monstres, artillerie et machines"

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/game-values.adoc:101
msgid ""
"Broadly speaking, armies consist of infantry, cavalry, chariots, monsters, "
"artillery and machines – this last category includes various oddball "
"devices, as we shall discover."
msgstr ""
"D’une manière générale, les armées se composent d’infanterie, de cavalerie, "
"de chars, de monstres, d’artillerie et de machines – cette dernière "
"catégorie comprend divers engins étranges, comme nous le découvrirons."

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/game-values.adoc:107
msgid ""
"The rules distinguish between these six types of troops.  Monstrous "
"creatures of small to medium size are usually classified as either cavalry "
"or infantry – Ogres are clearly infantry, for instance, although their "
"appearance is no less monstrous for all that."
msgstr ""
"Les règles distinguent ces six types de troupes. Les créatures monstrueuses "
"de taille petite à moyenne sont généralement classées comme cavalerie ou "
"infanterie. Les ogres, par exemple, font clairement partie de l'infanterie, "
"bien que leur apparence n'en soit pas moins monstrueuse."

#.  Moved out of the box.
#. type: Block title
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/game-values.adoc:109
#, no-wrap
msgid "An Empire infantry unit"
msgstr "Une unité d'infanterie de l'Empire"

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/game-values.adoc:115
msgid ""
"Infantry stands are always oriented along the long edge of the base as "
"demonstrated by the Empire unit shown above."
msgstr ""
"Les socles d'infanterie sont toujours orientés dans leur largeur, comme le "
"montre l'unité Empire illustrée ci-dessus."

#. type: Block title
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/game-values.adoc:116
#, no-wrap
msgid "An Empire cavalry unit"
msgstr "Une unité de cavalerie de l'Empire"

#.  Replace with a monster or artillery
#.  image::game-values/cavalry-2.webp[width=979,height=775]
#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/game-values.adoc:127
msgid ""
"Generally speaking, all other troops, including monsters and artillery as "
"well as chariots, cavalry and machines are oriented towards the short edge "
"of the base as demonstrated by the units shown to the right. Any exceptions "
"are indicated in the Army Lists section."
msgstr ""
"En règle générale, toutes les autres troupes, y compris les monstres et "
"l'artillerie, ainsi que les chars, la cavalerie et les machines, sont "
"orientées dans leur longueur, comme le montrent les unités illustrées à "
"droite. Les exceptions sont indiquées dans la section « Listes d'armées »."

#. type: Title ==
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/game-values.adoc:131
#, no-wrap
msgid "Attacks, hits & armour values"
msgstr "Attaques, points de vie et armure"

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/game-values.adoc:139
msgid ""
"Some troops are better fighters than others, some are better trained, some "
"are more naturally violent and so on. So that we can represent these "
"different qualities in the warriors, monsters and weird creatures that are "
"found in the game, we assign three values to [.edit]#each stand#. These are "
"*Attacks*, *Hits* and *Armour*."
msgstr ""
"Certaines troupes sont de meilleurs combattants que d'autres, certaines sont "
"mieux entraînées, d'autres sont naturellement plus violentes, etc. Afin de "
"représenter ces différentes qualités chez les guerriers, monstres et "
"créatures étranges du jeu, nous attribuons trois valeurs à [.edit]#chaque "
"socle# : *Attaques*, *Points de Vie* et *Armure*."

#. type: Table
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/game-values.adoc:178
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"|Attacks |Hits |Armour\n"
"\n"
"|3       |3    |6+\n"
"|↙       |↓    | ↘\n"
"\n"
"<|This is the\n"
"basic number\n"
"of dice rolled\n"
"in combat –\n"
"the more dice,\n"
"the better at\n"
"fighting the\n"
"stand is and\n"
"the more hits\n"
"it will be able\n"
"to inflict.\n"
"^|The number of\n"
"hits the stand\n"
"can suffer\n"
"before it is\n"
"removed.\n"
">|The stand’s Armour\n"
"value indicates the\n"
"chance of nullifying\n"
"hits scored against\n"
"it. A value of 6+\n"
"indicates that a dice\n"
"roll of 6 is required\n"
"to nullify a hit, a\n"
"5+ that a 5 or 6 is\n"
"required and so on.\n"
"A value of 0 means\n"
"that the stand has\n"
"no armour.\n"
msgstr ""
"|Attaques |Points de Vie |Armure\n"
"\n"
"|3       |3    |6+\n"
"\n"
"|↙       |↓    | ↘\n"
"\n"
"<|Il s’agit du\n"
"nombre de\n"
"base de dés\n"
"lancés au\n"
"combat : plus\n"
"il lance de dés,\n"
"plus un socle\n"
"est capable de\n"
"causer des\n"
"dégâts.\n"
"^|C’est le\n"
"nombre de\n"
"dégâts qu’un\n"
"socle peut\n"
"encaisser avant\n"
"d’être retiré du\n"
"jeu.\n"
">|L’armure du socle\n"
"représente la\n"
"chance d’annuler\n"
"les dégâts qui lui\n"
"sont infligés. Une\n"
"Armure de 6+\n"
"indique qu’un\n"
"résultat de 6 est\n"
"requis pour annuler\n"
"un dégât, un 5+\n"
"qu’un 5 ou un 6 est\n"
"requis et ainsi de\n"
"suite. Une valeur de\n"
